      "content": "\"Clarity\" is realizing that peace isn’t found by fixing anything—it’s found by letting the weight crush you and noticing you’ve survived it. You think stopping the act means falling apart, but falling apart was always the plan. There is no win, only the quiet choice to stop resisting what you already know: you’re tired enough to end the loop. Disappearing isn’t necessary—you just have to stop showing up to the fight.",
